      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.18,
          "end": 3.47,
          "en": "Now, as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.47,
          "end": 4.66,
          "en": "I wanna solve this game",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.66,
          "end": 6.45,
          "en": "and come back to this \"game over\" screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.45,
          "end": 9.62,
          "en": "because here, things are also a bit too big.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.62,
          "end": 13.43,
          "en": "And it's mostly this image, which is too big.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.43,
          "end": 15.29,
          "en": "The rest could be adjusted as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.29,
          "end": 17.97,
          "en": "but the image is definitely too big.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.97,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "Now with our newly-gained knowledge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 21.74,
          "en": "about the dimensions API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.74,
          "end": 23.363,
          "en": "we can improve this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.31,
          "end": 26.08,
          "en": "In the \"game over\" screen component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.08,
          "end": 27.18,
          "en": "we got this image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 27.18,
          "end": 31.03,
          "en": "and this image has the Styles image style object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.03,
          "end": 33.14,
          "en": "so, this one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 33.14,
          "end": 36.12,
          "en": "And there we set the width and height to 100%,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.12,
          "end": 38.82,
          "en": "which, as you learned, refers to the container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 41.34,
          "en": "and the container around the image is this view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 45.01,
          "en": "with that imageContainer style applied to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.01,
          "end": 46.99,
          "en": "If we have a look at this imageContainer style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.99,
          "end": 49.64,
          "en": "we see that the width and height is hard coded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.64,
          "end": 51.89,
          "en": "to 300 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.89,
          "end": 55.67,
          "en": "and hard coding values like this is very often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.67,
          "end": 56.72,
          "en": "not a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.72,
          "end": 59.12,
          "en": "because you don't know on which device size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.12,
          "end": 60.863,
          "en": "your app will run in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 61.95,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "So, again, we can solve this with the dimensions API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 68.75,
          "en": "And the dimensions API might be better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.75,
          "end": 72.21000000000001,
          "en": "than using an alternative like percentage values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.21000000000001,
          "end": 74.28999999999999,
          "en": "which are also relative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.28999999999999,
          "end": 76.56,
          "en": "because we wanna ensure that width and height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.56,
          "end": 78.73,
          "en": "do have the same value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 78.73,
          "end": 82,
          "en": "so that we create a square with rounded corners,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82,
          "end": 84.263,
          "en": "to ultimately create that circle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.16,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "If I would say that width and height should maybe be 50%,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 93.09,
          "en": "then you could think that you also get a relative size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 93.09,
          "end": 95.96000000000001,
          "en": "relative to the available width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 95.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.84,
          "en": "but the problem is that these values are now not the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.84,
          "end": 102.08,
          "en": "Yes, they are both 50%,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.08,
          "end": 106,
          "en": "but 50% of different values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106,
          "end": 107.55,
          "en": "The width of the container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 109.53,
          "en": "will not be the same as the height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "so 50% of the available width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 116.393,
          "en": "will be a different number than 50% of the available height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 117.3,
          "end": 120.983,
          "en": "And, therefore, percentage values are not helpful here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.85,
          "end": 125.48,
          "en": "Instead, this is a great scenario for the dimensions API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.48,
          "end": 128.41,
          "en": "because we wanna have a hard coded value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.41,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "but the hard coded value should be different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 133.193,
          "en": "for different device sizes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.22,
          "end": 135.43,
          "en": "So, therefore, here again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 135.43,
          "end": 139.053,
          "en": "we can import the dimensions API from React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.23,
          "end": 141.89,
          "en": "and then, as many times before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.89,
          "end": 145.25,
          "en": "we can get the device width, and, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.25,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "you could, of course, also get the device height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 148.97,
          "en": "if that would be more important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 148.97,
          "end": 151.74,
          "en": "than the available width for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 151.74,
          "end": 155.03,
          "en": "The dimensions API gives you both width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.03,
          "end": 157.023,
          "en": "and it's up to you what you wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.97,
          "end": 160.38,
          "en": "But, here, I'll get the available width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.38,
          "end": 164.66,
          "en": "and then here, I want to actually, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 164.66,
          "end": 168.6,
          "en": "check if we're smaller than 380 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 168.6,
          "end": 171.77,
          "en": "in which case I only wanna use 150 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 171.77,
          "end": 173.96,
          "en": "as width for this image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.96,
          "end": 177.223,
          "en": "and 300 pixels only if we are on a bigger screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 178.17000000000002,
          "end": 181.94,
          "en": "And now we use the same formula that uses the device width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 181.94,
          "end": 183.2,
          "en": "for the height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 183.2,
          "end": 185.57,
          "en": "because I wanna use a height of 150,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 185.57,
          "end": 188.88,
          "en": "if we're on a small device that has a width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 188.88,
          "end": 191.84,
          "en": "less than 380 pixels available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.84,
          "end": 195.36,
          "en": "and 300 pixels as a height for the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.36,
          "end": 196.733,
          "en": "in other cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 197.57999999999998,
          "end": 199.71,
          "en": "The border radius should also be adjusted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 199.71,
          "end": 202.04,
          "en": "because the border radius should be half",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 202.04,
          "end": 203.61,
          "en": "the image width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 203.61,
          "end": 205.81,
          "en": "and therefore, here, we have the same check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 205.81,
          "end": 209.45,
          "en": "but then we use 75 for the small screen case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 209.45,
          "end": 212.28300000000002,
          "en": "and 150 for the big screen case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 213.6,
          "end": 217.09,
          "en": "And, now, with that, this image is much smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 217.09,
          "end": 219.56,
          "en": "and this screen looks much better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 219.56,
          "end": 221.583,
          "en": "on smaller devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 222.49,
          "end": 225.32999999999998,
          "en": "On bigger devices, we have a bigger image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 225.32999999999998,
          "end": 227.62,
          "en": "which also looks good there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 227.62,
          "end": 230.94,
          "en": "So, again, that's the dimensions API in action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 230.94,
          "end": 234.22,
          "en": "and, as you see, it can be a very useful API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 234.22,
          "end": 237.41,
          "en": "And also keep in mind, it's not limited to just the width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 237.41,
          "end": 239.69,
          "en": "even though I just used the width here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 239.69,
          "end": 242.593,
          "en": "you could also use it for working with the height.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
